 131: /**
 132:  * The cash shop, in the game's own 190x429 item window.
 133:  *
 134:  * It is the NPC shop with Jewels of Chaos for zen: the same grid of 20px
 135:  * squares, the same item icons and tooltips, the same money bar on the bottom
 136:  * edge. A player who can read a merchant can read this without being taught
 137:  * anything.
 138:  *
 139:  * No sign-in. The player is already logged in - the window opens off the item
 140:  * shop button on the bottom bar - and the service names them from the nonce
 141:  * their game socket carries (state.ts), so nothing is ever typed twice.
 142:  *
 143:  * Nothing bought here lands in the bag while this window is open: the shop
 144:  * only ever writes to an account the game server does not have in memory, so
 145:  * an order waits for the player to log out. The fifth tab says so, in one
 146:  * sentence, above the queue, because a purchase that does not appear reads
 147:  * as a bug to anyone who has not been told.
 148:  *
 149:  * A roll is drawn on the press but only sent once its order is delivered
 150:  * (cashshop/server/orders.ts `forPlayer`), so the gacha is drawn in two
 151:  * halves. Nothing in the sealed half may differ by tier - a single tell would
 152:  * let a player who dislikes what they see spend their jewels before logging
 153:  * out, fail the delivery, and get the daily-cap slot back to roll again - so
 154:  * everything the stage reads off a roll is behind `isOpening`, and a shut box
 155:  * wears `SEALED_TINT` and `SEALED_COLOUR` whatever is in it.
 156:  */
