 745:   // The bar draws what the next order can spend, never the bag as it is: the
 746:   // jewels for an order leave the bag at delivery, which is after logout, so
 747:   // the live inventory does not move when a purchase is taken. Drawing it
 748:   // unchanged would let a player buy the same jewels twice on screen and be
 749:   // refused for the second; drawing it decremented locally would be a lie
 750:   // about what is in the bag. So the count shown is the service's wallet -
 751:   // bag plus vault at the last save - minus what the queue has promised, and
 752:   // beside it, when anything is promised, how much is held. The bag count is
 753:   // only the fallback before the service has said who we are.
 754:   const spendable = chaosToSpend(items);
 755:   const held = committedChaos();
