 37: /**
 38:  * `CNewUIMiniMap` (NewUIMiniMap.cpp): TAB drops a near-black sheet over the
 39:  * play area and draws the world's `mini_map.ozt` rotated 45° so that the
 40:  * hero sits at the centre, with the NPC and portal markers from the
 41:  * localised `Minimap_World{n}.bmd` riding on it. Hovering a marker shows its
 42:  * name in a tip box, the X at the top right (or TAB / ESC) closes it, and
 43:  * while it is open every other hot key is swallowed (`NewUIHotKey.cpp:131`).
 44:  *
 45:  * Geometry, in the original's 640×480 UI space: the sheet is 640×430 (the
 46:  * main frame stays visible under it), the map is `m_Lenth[m_MiniPos]` px on
 47:  * a side (800 at the only zoom level the original ever uses; the other five
 48:  * entries are here as the mouse-wheel zoom, which is ours) and the hero's
 49:  * tile is pinned to the screen centre - texture U runs along tile Y and V
 50:  * along tile X (`Tx = PositionY / 256 · L`, `Ty = PositionX / 256 · L`).
 51:  * Markers are 15 px (NPC) / 30 px (portal) sprites placed at their tile the
 52:  * same way and spun by their own `Rotation` on top of the map's 45°.
 53:  * `RenderPointRotate` nudges every marker 25 px right and the hero sprite is
 54:  * drawn at (325, 230) rather than (320, 240); both read as fudge against
 55:  * `ConvertX`, so here everything shares the exact centre.
 56:  *
 57:  * Ours on top: click and drag slides the map off the hero, and a Center
 58:  * button next to the X (shown only while off it) brings it back. The TAB
 59:  * and Escape keys are handled by `Minimap` (`index.tsx`).
 60:  */
 61: 
 62: const SHEET_WIDTH = 640;
 63: const SHEET_HEIGHT = 430;
 64: const SHEET_ALPHA = 0.85;
 65: const CENTER_X = 320;
 66: const CENTER_Y = 240;
 67: 
 68: /** `m_Lenth[]`: map edge length per zoom step. */
 69: const ZOOM_LEVELS = [800, 1000, 1200, 1400, 1600, 1800];
